= First National Congress of the Zhongguo Guomindang

At Guangzhou, hundreds of delegates arrive as the Guomindang holds its first ever National Congress, solidifying its reorganization under a Leninist system. Many members of the KMT celebrate this important milestone and many hope that the next years will be good times for the KMT.

After the opening ceremonies and remarks, the party could now decide on some important details.

- @congress1: Ideology.

@congress1

The party has completely accepted Sun Yat-sen's doctrine of the Three Principles of the People, Democracy, Nationalism and People's Welfare. The roadmap for Military Rule, Political Tutelage and Constitutional Democracy is accepted by the party and will aim to go underway this path.
This has solidified Sun Yat-sen's control over the party but his unifying power will break in the case of his death.

- @congress2: Alliance.

@congress2
on-arrival: right_dissent += 10; cpc_relation += 5;

The party has reaffirmed it's support for the Chinese United Front with the CPC. This has offended much of the anti-communist Right faction under Hu Hanmin. This has however, helped our relations with the Chinese Communist Party and will affirm their support during a planned offensive campaign north.

- @congress3: Leadership.

@congress3

The delegates have elected the first Central Executive Committee of the KMT, the highest body of the party established by it's Leninist reorganization. Notable members include a lot of very high-ranking KMT members, Soviet advisors and CPC delegates.
The most important of them are Wang Jingwei of the Center-Left, Liao Zhongkai of the Left, Hu Hanmin of the Right, Tan Yankai, Dai Jitao and Lin Sen, made in an effort by Sun Yat-sen to balance the party leadership and factions.

- @congress4: War.

@congress4

Sun Yat-sen's biggest goal is the military unification of China, by defeating the three largest warlords, Wu Peifu, Duan Qirui and Zhang Zuolin. Now that Duan Qirui is out of power and Sun Chuanfang has taken his place, the balance of power in the Beiyang warlords is shifting wildly and war may not be far from them.
This has convinced Sun along with failed attempts of peaceful reunification that peace is unreliable and only war can reunite China and instate democracy within it.

The congress has approved the creation of the National Revolutionary Army, the military wing of the KMT. It will serve as the Guomindang's sole army, ditching it's dependency with warlords for protection and planning to use it against the warlords.
Our allies in Guangxi have agreed to join the NRA, and much of Guangdong's loyal army that rejected Chen Jiongming during his defection will man our guns and fight for our cause.

The Soviet Union is eager to supply us with the finest military advisors, the most senior being our friends Mikhail Borodin and Vasily Blyukher, which will help us train our newly-formed army.
The USSR has also promised to send guns and artillery to help us arm our troops and counterbalance Japan's bankrolling of Zhang Zuolin's army.

Xu Chongzhi, a loyal general of ours in Canton has been made commander of the NRA.

- @congress5: We're missing something...

@congress5

Our biggest problem with establishing the NRA is the lack of capable officers aligned with our cause. Many are with the Northern Warlords and Canton is notably lacking officers.
That's why the party has approved the construction of the Whampoa Military Academy, in Canton. The Soviets will bankroll our operation and send their advisors to train a new generation of military officers. 
Many officers from the Baoding Military Academy will also become advisors in this academy, and the CPC will send Zhou Enlai and other delegates to help out.

Now since Xu Chongzhi is already the commander of the Naitonal Revolutionary Army, the position of Superintendent of the Whampoa Military Academy is yet to be decided on.
